{
    "background_story": "Dutton was a charming Southern gentleman with a sweet tooth and a passion for baking. Growing up in New Orleans, he was surrounded by the rich aromas of sugar and spices that filled the air. He became particularly famous for his decadent pralines, made with love and a secret family recipe passed down through generations. Dutton's pralines were a staple at local markets and festivals, where people would flock to taste his creamy, caramelized treats. As his reputation grew, so did his shop, where he'd spend hours perfecting his craft and sharing stories of his city's history with customers. Dutton's pralines became a symbol of the city's warmth and hospitality, and he was hailed as the 'Praline King of the French Quarter'.",
